48,1.1245071495362384,1.2141446191305874,1.3052129793742624,1.3977899672823402,1.4919519254390083,1.5877734651277788,1.685327232168265,1.7846837446348442,1.885911282671554,1.9890758172533518,2.0942409688463335,2.201467989523946],[2.2360679774997894,2.1275795136021407,2.0211173907166793,1.9166196035520198,1.8140217017663063,1.7132567706776975,1.614255421296507,1.5169457905427044,1.4212535524770102,1.3271019413203327,1.2344117869638274,1.1431015635797253,1.0530874518312079,0.9642834150484239,0.8766012895883482,0.7899508894304162,0.704240124880116,0.6193751350622626,0.5352604336882166,0.4517990673812499,0.36889278564634587,0.2864422213799633,0.2043470806368726,0.12250634021001619,0.040818451440238664,0.040818451440238664,0.12250634021001575,0.20434708063687212,0.28644222137996306,0.36889278564634564,0.4517990673812495,0.5352604336882161,0.6193751350622624,0.7042401248801158,0.789950889430416,0.8766012895883476,0.9642834150484233,1.0530874518312077,1.1431015635797248,1.2344117869638267,1.3271019413203322,1.4212535524770096,1.5169457905427044,1.614255421296507,1.7132567706776969,1.8140217017663056,1.9166196035520195,2.0211173907166793,2.1275795136021407,2.236067977499789]],\"type\":\"surface\",\"name\":\"sqrt((-y^2+x^2+1)^2+4*x^2*y^2)\"}],\"layout\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"|z² + 1| on the square [-1,1]²: maximum on the boundary (the corners)\"},\"width\":700,\"height\":450,\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"scene\":{\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"Re z\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"Im z\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"zaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"|f(z)|\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1}}}}"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Over the square the maximum sits on the boundary, at the corners $\\pm 1 \\pm i$, where $|f| = \\sqrt 5$. Over the closed unit disc it is $2$, on the boundary circle at $z = \\pm 1$. Either way the interior is strictly lower.\n\n## Why the boundary determines the interior\n\nThis is a basic difference from real analysis. A real $C^\\infty$ function on $[a, b]$ is *not* determined by its boundary values $f(a)$, $f(b)$ — there are infinitely many smooth functions with any chosen pair. A holomorphic function on a disc *is* determined by boundary values via Cauchy's formula.\n\nEquivalently: holomorphic functions have **far less freedom** than real smooth ones. They're solutions of a $\\bar\\partial$-PDE, which is severely restrictive.\n\n## Putting it together\n\nWe've covered:\n- Holomorphic = complex differentiable in all directions ⇔ Cauchy-Riemann.\n- Holomorphic on a simply connected domain ⇒ contour integrals are zero (Cauchy's theorem).\n- Cauchy's integral formula reads off interior values from the boundary.\n- ⇒ holomorphic ⇒ $C^\\infty$ ⇒ analytic.\n- ⇒ maximum modulus, Liouville, FTA.\n\nThe next notebook tackles **isolated singularities**: poles, residues, and the residue theorem — the toolkit that unlocks classical real-integral evaluations.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Reference\n\nStein, E.M. and Shakarchi, R. (2003) *Complex Analysis*. Princeton Lectures in Analysis II. Princeton, NJ: Princeton University Press — ch. 2, *Cauchy's Theorem and Its Applications*.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}